        "title": "TCP Flow Control & Congestion Control",
        "approved": true,
        "approved_by": "lecturer@ictu.edu.vn",
        "student_safe_content": "TCP flow control uses a sliding receive window (rwnd) advertised by the receiver so the sender never overflows the receiver buffer. TCP congestion control dynamically adapts the congestion window (cwnd) via slow start, congestion avoidance, and multiplicative decrease after packet loss.",
